    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10353": {
      "title": "Director of Philanthropy",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Director of Philanthropy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Philanthropy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Philanthropy Position Class Type Regular Position Type Staff Other Position Information About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. Benefits: include health, dental and vision coverage; retirement benefits with up to a 9% Kettering matching contribution; life and accident insurance; tuition assistance and waiver programs; vacation and holiday pay; sick and disability pay; home purchase assistance program; recreation center membership; and many other benefits. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. Position Status Full-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications - Job Specific Required Qualifications -Bachelor’s degree required; -Minimum 3 years of proven fund raising experience and a successful track record in gift solicitation OR 2 to 5 years related experience in industry with preference given to those with deep institutional knowledge of Kettering University; -Disciplined self-starter who regularly sets and achieves work goals; -Exceptional organizational, interpersonal, and networking skills with large groups as well as individuals; -Excellent verbal and written communication skills required; -Ability to work well in a small team environment; -Knowledge of engineering and the ability to close solicitations; -Must be willing to travel and work irregular hours as needed. Understanding and commitment to Kettering University Values a. RESPECT : for teamwork, honesty, encouragement, diversity partnerships with students. b. INTEGRITY : including accountability, transparency and ethics. c. CREATIVITY : fostering flexibility and innovation. d. COLLABORATION : across disciplines and with all partners. e. EXCELLENCE : in all we do. Special Event Expectations: Participation and assistance is expected at major campus special events, such as commencement. Posting Information Posting Number SP00491 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 85 Duties Oversee a portfolio of existing individual donors and identify new prospective donors to cultivate, solicit, and steward. Cultivate existing individual donors and encourage renewal and increased donor support. Collaborate with other staff on rating, solicitation and stewardship strategies. Percent of total time 10 Duties Participate in planning and staffing fundraising and friend-raising events. Percent of total time 5 Duties Support the overall work of the University Advancement office including Alumni Engagement, Special Events, Corporate and Foundation Giving, and External Relations. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please provide the specific name of the publication or website where you learned about this posting. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
