    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10335": {
      "title": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Custodian and Groundskeeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian and Groundskeeper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Custodian and Groundskeeper Position Class Type Regular Position Type Staff Other Position Information About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. Benefits: include health, dental and vision coverage; retirement benefits with up to a 9% Kettering matching contribution; life and accident insurance; tuition assistance and waiver programs; vacation and holiday pay; sick and disability pay; home purchase assistance program; recreation center membership; and many other benefits. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. Position Status Full-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications -Demonstrated effective interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. -Demonstrated ability to use computer. -Knowledge of electronic email and work order system. -Ordering of custodial supplies for building(s). Job Specific Required Qualifications -Ability to perform the job functions for an eight (8) hour day, five (5) days a week to include: standing, walking, bending, kneeling, stooping, stretching, lifting up to 50 lbs., reaching, pulling, pushing, carrying, climbing, jumping, running, sitting, sweeping, climbing stairs, working outdoors, and safely handling power equipment. -Ability to successfully complete online Bloodborne Pathogens and all other required training. -Demonstrated initiative and good independent judgment. -Experience in training other custodians in methods and equipment operation and care. -Experience in team/project coordination. Understanding and commitment to Kettering University Values a. RESPECT : for teamwork, honesty, encouragement, diversity partnerships with students. b. INTEGRITY : including accountability, transparency and ethics. c. CREATIVITY : fostering flexibility and innovation. d. COLLABORATION : across disciplines and with all partners. e. EXCELLENCE : in all we do. Posting Information Posting Number SP00488 Posting Date 08/24/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 25 Duties Perform custodial work involved in care and cleaning of specified area or areas of a building including: restrooms, stairways, chalk boards/whiteboards, locker rooms, classrooms, laboratories, offices, shops, etc. Percent of total time 20 Duties Perform all phases of floor, wall, ceiling and glass care and cleaning. Percent of total time 10 Duties Perform safe operation, care and cleaning of custodial equipment. Percent of total time 10 Duties Coordinate work schedules and special assignments for assigned group, inspect quality of work performed as well as provide input to supervisor regarding employee performance. Percent of total time 5 Duties Train other custodians in proper methods and operation of equipment. Percent of total time 5 Duties Assist in room/event set up and breakdown. Percent of total time 5 Duties Assist groundkeeping staff as assigned including snow and weed removal. Percent of total time 5 Duties Maintain inventory and supplies. Percent of total time 5 Duties Performs other duties as assigned or requested. Percent of total time 5 Duties Coordinate with co-worker(s) to provide proper coverage when needed. Percent of total time 5 Duties Comply with University safety and security policies and procedures and report conditions that may create hazards. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please provide the specific name of the publication or website where you learned about this posting. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
